  "body": "What happens: #1445 slice 2 found that the Fanuc-family posts wrote `P<ms>` on G86, and the published Fanuc G86 format has no P word. The dwell was dropped without a message. The same risk can apply to G83 (deep peck): some controls read P on G83, some do not.\n\nExpected: a post writes a dwell only on a cycle whose published format has a dwell word on that control. Otherwise the post refuses the dwell by name.\n\nEvidence: `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`, `haas.cps`, `mazak.cps`, `doosan-dnm.cps`, the `onCycle` cycle map. Check the public operator manuals for the G83 address words.\n\nDone means: each Fanuc-family post either writes the G83 dwell where the published format has it, or refuses a G83 dwell by name. A test pins it.\n\nPart of #1445\n",
